## Reproduction playbook

1. TODO: Freeze source/checkpoint/package versions, environment and input hashes.
   Inspect installation and license boundaries before executing anything.
2. TODO: Validate one small known case, its outputs and its failure path. Separate
   a proposed smoke test from a test actually performed and archived.
3. TODO: Compare the matched control under the same workload, splits, resource
   limits, timing boundaries and tuning budget. Save raw repetitions and failures.
4. TODO: Define acceptance and rollback criteria before inspecting test outcomes.
   For models, keep validation selection separate from frozen OOD test evaluation.

Do not call a command sequence complete or reproducible while required inputs,
data modules or configuration keys are missing. Exact resolved pins are not
version ranges. Never invent runtime, VRAM, throughput or completion-time claims.

## Pre-publication audit

- [ ] The lead answers the actual question in 40–60 words.
- [ ] Sources support the mechanism, quoted wording and strongest conclusions.
- [ ] All measured, reported, illustrative and unverified values are distinguished.
- [ ] Commands/configs are tested with archived outputs or explicitly unexecuted.
- [ ] Rights, authorization, secrets, data privacy and recovery boundaries are clear.
- [ ] Registered figures and their prose/text equivalents agree.
- [ ] The verdict names a use case, a rejection condition and remaining uncertainty.
- [ ] Add 3–5 real FAQ entries in frontmatter only when useful; the page owns FAQ rendering.
- [ ] Remove every TODO and inspect draft status before an author-approved publication.

